    "body": "`shared_cache` is reused across both `inst.reachable_functions(32, ...)` and `inst.reachable_functions(64, ...)`. The reachable-functions analysis depends on `__effective_xlen`/`xlen` via the symbol table, but the cache key in `Idl::FunctionCallExpressionAst#reachable_functions` is only `[name, tvals, avals]`, so results computed under XLEN=32 can be incorrectly reused under XLEN=64 (and vice versa). Consider partitioning the cache by `effective_xlen` (e.g., separate caches per base) or incorporating the effective XLEN into the cache key.",
